-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project is infrastructure for structuring work on coding assessments —
both manual and AI-assisted. The ideas, patterns, and general approach are
freely available to study, learn from, and adapt.

However, the value of this repo as evidence of capability lies in its author
having designed and built it: the prompt engineering, the test harness, the
benchmark-driven selection workflow. Someone who submits this infrastructure
as-is — or with only superficial changes — as part of their own assessment
would be misrepresenting the source of that effort. The scaffolding did not
come from them.

If you are using this repo in the context of a coding assessment or interview,
the expectation is that you build your own harness, or at least that the
harness you use reflects your own thinking. The solutions and test cases inside
it are, by design, not checked in — they are yours to write. The infrastructure
around them should be too.

